e updated during fine-tuning, potentially reducing training time and preventing overfitting."], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Further Pre-training on Financial Corpus': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The process of training a language model, such as FinBERT, on a large dataset of financial text to improve its understanding of financial vocabulary and context.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'LSTM network': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A type of recurrent neural network used for processing sequential data, such as text, and is used in the text to classify sentences from financial news according to their sentiment.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'word2vec': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method for generating word embeddings, which are vector representations of words, used to capture semantic relationships between words.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'SST-5': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used for text classification tasks, mentioned in the context of evaluating the performance of models using word embeddings.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Text simplification': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A technique used in conjunction with an LSTM network to classify sentences from financial news based on their sentiment.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'ELMo': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method for generating contextualized word embeddings, which are used to improve performance on various NLP tasks. The text mentions its use in conjunction with contextualized word embeddings.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'LSTM': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['Long short-term memory (LSTM) is a type of recurrent neural network that allows long-term dependencies in a sequence to persist in the network by using "forget" and "update" gates.', 'A baseline method used for sentiment analysis, implemented and compared against FinBERT.', 'A baseline method, Long Short-Term Memory, a type of recurrent neural network used for sequence modeling, implemented and compared against FinBERT.', 'A type of recurrent neural network used as a baseline classifier in the study.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 8, 8, 9]}, 'Natural Language Inference': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A natural language processing task that involves determining the logical relationship between two sentences.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Question Answering': {'type': ['task', 'task'], 'description': ['A natural language processing task that involves answering questions posed in natural language.', 'A natural language processing task that involves building systems capable of answering questions posed in natural language, applicable within the financial domain.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3, 11]}, 'Text classification': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ["The task of categorizing text into predefined classes, relevant to the document's focus on sentiment analysis."], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'Bidirectional language model': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A type of language model that considers context from both preceding and following words in a sequence, which is a key concept in the document.'], 'source_chunk_index': [3]}, 'AWD-LSTM': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['The underlying language model used in ULMFit, employing sophisticated dropout tuning strategies to regularize its LSTM model.', 'The underlying language model used in ULMFit, employing dropout tuning strategies for regularization.', 'A language model, mentioned in contrast to BERT, which defines the language modeling task differently.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 4, 5]}, 'Transformer': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['An attention-based architecture for modeling sequential information, presented as an alternative to recurrent neural networks.', 'An attention-based architecture for modeling sequential information, presented as an alternative to recurrent neural networks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 4]}, 'ULMFit': {'type': ['method', 'method', 'method', 'method', 'method'], 'description': ['A transfer learning model for down-stream NLP tasks, utilizing language model pre-training.', 'A baseline method used for sentiment analysis, implemented and compared against FinBERT.', 'A baseline method, Universal Language Model Fine-tuning, used for transfer learning and compared against FinBERT.', 'A transfer learning method used for comparison with FinBERT.', 'A pre-training language model used for comparison with FinBERT in the context of financial NLP tasks.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4, 8, 8, 9, 11]}, 'Recurrent Neural Networks (RNNs)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A class of neural networks that are sequential in nature, making them harder to parallelize on GPUs. They also face challenges in maintaining information across long sequences.'], 'source_chunk_index': [4]}, 'Next Sentence Prediction': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['A task that BERT is trained on, which involves predicting whether a given sentence follows another in the original text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [5]}, 'BERT': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A bidirectional transformer-based language model used as the foundation for FinBERT. It has two versions: BERT-base and BERT-large, differing in the number of encoder layers, hidden size, multi-head attention heads, and parameters.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'BookCorpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used for pre-training BERT, containing a large collection of books.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'English Wikipedia': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A dataset used for pre-training BERT, comprising the content of the English Wikipedia.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Domain Corpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['The specific financial corpus used for further pre-training of FinBERT, though the exact name is not provided in this text unit.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Classification Tasks': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The general category of tasks for which FinBERT is being implemented, including sentiment analysis, as described in the priming summary.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'Regression Tasks': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The general category of tasks for which FinBERT is being implemented, though the specific regression tasks are not described in this text unit.'], 'source_chunk_index': [6]}, 'LSTM classifier with GLoVe embeddings': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method used as a baseline for comparison, employing a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) classifier with Global Vectors for Word Representation (GloVe) embeddings.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'LSTM classifier with ELMo embeddings': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method used as a baseline for comparison, employing a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) classifier with Embeddings from Language Models (ELMo) embeddings.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'ULMFit classifier': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method used as a baseline for comparison, employing a Universal Language Model Fine-tuning (ULMFit) classifier.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'TRC 2 financial corpus': {'type': ['dataset'], 'description': ['A financial corpus used for pre-training the AWD-LSTM language model in the ULMFit method.'], 'source_chunk_index': [7]}, 'LPS': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A machine learning model used for sentiment analysis, serving as a baseline for comparison with FinBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'HSC': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A machine learning model used for sentiment analysis, serving as a baseline for comparison with FinBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'FinSSLX': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A model that incorporates text simplification and pre-training of word embeddings on a large financial corpus with sentiment labels, used for comparison with FinBERT.'], 'source_chunk_index': [8]}, 'Vanilla BERT': {'type': [